# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-safe-recoveries.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/573-accept-a-merge-of-origin-main-as-a-valid-implement-result-in-publication-proof/requirements.md
Feature: Accept a merge of origin/main as a valid implement result in publication proof

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A merge-of-main tip passes the subject proof
    Given an issue branch with a pushed "fix: repair the parser (#N)" commit
    And the branch tip is a pushed merge of origin/main that brings in another issue's specs directory
    When reconcile runs for implement with the subject "fix: repair the parser (#N)"
    Then it passes without an issue-subject commit at the tip

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Files from the default branch are outside the scope check
    Given an in-progress merge of origin/main that stages another issue's specs/<M>-*/ files
    And the resolved tree changes only paths the issue may change
    When bind runs for implement with the issue's implementation subject
    Then it passes
    And only the diff between the merged-in main commit and the working tree was checked

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Real out-of-scope changes are still refused
    Given a merge of origin/main whose result also edits <path>, which main does not change
    When <command> runs for implement
    Then it is refused

    Examples:
      | path                                     | command   |
      | another issue's specs/<M>-*/design.md    | bind      |
      | this issue's Approved requirements.md    | reconcile |
